Debian 13 update (2026-10-02)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Qore gRPC module packages
========================

This is a development snapshot for qore-testing, not a final release.
The native Arrow schema/IPC/record-batch implementation links to distribution
libarrow. GrpcUtil, GrpcDataProvider, ArrowFlightDataProvider and
SalesforcePubSubDataProvider ship as source and AOT modules, with metadata,
resources and all translation catalogs. The doc package contains five API
references and complete test fixtures. Test TLS keys are PUBLIC TEST IDENTITIES
and must never be used for real deployments.

Build natively with dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc and the matching Qore 3 SDK.
No network downloads are performed during builds. Arch-only, indep-only,
nocheck and nodoc profiles are supported; cross builds require a separate
host SDK and are rejected. Fixed qcc partitions and preserved AOT trailers
support reproducible builds and fresh-process compilation. Provider build
dependencies ensure GrpcUtil is compiled before its consumers.

Tests use local Qore/Python servers and distribution grpcio, grpc-tools and
PyArrow, plus the separately packaged Qore process module. Required test
dependencies are checked before running the suites. Python protobuf stubs
are regenerated from test/test.proto in a disposable build test tree; no
generated test stubs, Python caches or binary dependencies ship.
Installed autopkgtests copy fixtures to a temporary directory without checkout
module paths and compile a fresh SDK client. The two interoperability scripts
also report an explicit QUnit skip if process is unavailable to source users.

Optional grpcurl interoperability tests skip if that command is unavailable;
it is not in the target distribution repositories. Live Salesforce checks
require an explicitly configured org; offline fixtures cover the provider
without contacting an account. Record all skips rather than counting them as
coverage. Package qualification alone does not certify live Salesforce access
or every Flight/reflection protocol feature.

Before general publication, qualify other Debian/Ubuntu releases and
architectures, freeze the Qore ABI/dependency versions and test relevant
upgrades. Testing PPA publication requires the matching Qore SDK and process
package. Source signing/upload and Launchpad publication are separate steps.
